\* All TLC check configs for AntflyDbSplitVisibility.tla, one section per check.
\* Sections are verbatim TLC config syntax; the build extracts them
\* (scripts/tla-cfg.sh). Section names match the make-target check ids.

==== positive
\* TLC config for AntflyDbSplitVisibility.tla

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyParentAcceptsChildAfterCutover = FALSE
    BuggyChildServesBeforeReplay = FALSE
    BuggyDonorServesAfterMerge = FALSE
    BuggyEnrichmentWrongOwner = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    RightOwnershipMatchesPhase
    RoutesCurrentOwner
    SplitDeltasTracked
    ParentCannotAcceptChildRangeAfterCutover
    ChildServingRequiresReplayAndIndexes
    ChildArtifactRemoteAfterSplit
    EnrichmentOnlyForCurrentRightOwner
    MergeDonorDoesNotServeAfterHandoff
    MergeReceiverRoutesAllIndexes
    Safety

==== BadChildServe
\* Expected-failure config: child range serves before replaying split deltas
\* and completing text/sparse/graph shadow indexes.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyParentAcceptsChildAfterCutover = FALSE
    BuggyChildServesBeforeReplay = TRUE
    BuggyDonorServesAfterMerge = FALSE
    BuggyEnrichmentWrongOwner = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    ChildServingRequiresReplayAndIndexes
    Safety

==== BadEnrichmentOwner
\* Expected-failure config: generated enrichment publishes under a stale or
\* otherwise non-owning right-range owner.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyParentAcceptsChildAfterCutover = FALSE
    BuggyChildServesBeforeReplay = FALSE
    BuggyDonorServesAfterMerge = FALSE
    BuggyEnrichmentWrongOwner = TRUE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    EnrichmentOnlyForCurrentRightOwner
    Safety

==== BadMergeDonor
\* Expected-failure config: merge donor still serves right-range writes after
\* receiver cutover.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyParentAcceptsChildAfterCutover = FALSE
    BuggyChildServesBeforeReplay = FALSE
    BuggyDonorServesAfterMerge = TRUE
    BuggyEnrichmentWrongOwner = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    MergeDonorDoesNotServeAfterHandoff
    Safety

==== BadParentWrite
\* Expected-failure config: parent accepts a right-range write after split
\* cutover transferred ownership to the child.

SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTANTS
    BuggyParentAcceptsChildAfterCutover = TRUE
    BuggyChildServesBeforeReplay = FALSE
    BuggyDonorServesAfterMerge = FALSE
    BuggyEnrichmentWrongOwner = FALSE

INVARIANTS
    TypeOK
    ParentCannotAcceptChildRangeAfterCutover
    Safety
